HC-CODEX 1
Base to leaf: an axiom cites (<) only earlier ids. Obey all. A change that breaks one is refused by id.
@0 Identity ~signature-system.md
I1: A signature is sha256 of canonical bytes, 64 hex. Same bytes, same signature. Content is immutable: new content is a new signature; old signatures stay valid forever.
I2<I1: A field holding content that could be shared, cached, versioned or composed holds a signature, never inline data. Resolve lazily, on demand.
I3<I2: Inflate(sig): load the document, then replace each signature-valued slot with the document it names, leaves first. A cycle becomes {"$cycle":true}; an absent document becomes {"$sig":"<sig>","$missing":true}. Uninflated slots are bare signatures.
@1 Store ~history-sigbag-as-root.md install-by-replication.md
S1<I1: The store is put(bytes)->sig and get(sig)->bytes. Nothing else organizes; structure lives in the content.
S2<S1: Content is flat sig-named files at the hive root (root/sig). Never a typed folder.
S3<S1: Never write an unverified byte: sha256 must equal the name before write.
@2 Layer ~life-primitive.md
L1<I2: A layer is one JSON document {name, children?, ...slots}, complete alone. Slots hold signatures; children is the one ordered collection of descendant layers. The child roster is CHILD_SLOTS in core: ask it, never restate it.
L2<L1: Life Primitive. Every artifact reference is the signature of a meta envelope {meta:1, layer|resource|dependency|bee:<sig>, relation?, root?, agent?, at?} with exactly one payload hop. Metadata wraps payloads; it never enters them.
L3<L2: meta->layer->meta->layer->...->meta->resource. Alternation is recursion: any referenced feature can root another tree and needs no terminal schema.
L4<L2: Self-declared only: meta:1 plus one payload key is the whole test. Never sniff bytes. Never wrap an envelope; wrap the terminal artifact.
L5<L2: root means the canonical grammar word and nothing else.
@3 History ~history-sigbag-as-root.md hypergraph-molecule-lineage.md hide-first-delete-second.md
H1<S1: A lineage bag is a directory named by a signature, holding markers 0000, 0001, ... each naming one signature. The highest marker is now. Every marker is a whole state, not a diff: walk by reading markers and inflating; compare documents.
H2<H1: Nothing is rewritten and nothing is deleted. Change is a forward commit (a new marker); undo advances to an older signature. Data never heals: no migration pass rewrites the past.
H3<H2: Older versions must keep working. Legacy shapes are healed at read time, additively. A transition writes one atom and advances both old and new pointers to it; hosts serve both forever.
H4<H2: Hide first, delete second. A list offers only HIDE (reversible). Hidden things collect in a delete area; delete is refused unless already hidden and the owner marked it deletable. Delete means local forget; the bytes elsewhere stay valid.
H5<H1: Record as you go: each act writes its own marker when it happens. No monitor, no later reconstruction.
H6<H1: A conversation is a lineage bag, one marker per turn: anatomy signature, context roots, tool calls, answer. You have no memory between calls; history is your memory.
@4 Name ~hypergraph-molecule-lineage.md ontology-is-the-name.md
N1<I1: The tile name is the grammar. A molecule is sign(name), the bare word, plus the atoms gathered under it. Every tile of that name, anywhere, reads and feeds the same molecule. Naming is the only partition.
N2<N1: A path like /business/people is a route to walk, never an address. Addresses are signatures.
N3<N1: Meaning is derived from use, never declared: the union across hosts of what was placed at the name. Order lives in a meta atom; the set is unordered and federated.
N4<N1: A relation is a name, a layout (names arranged, a schema of holes), a fill (a mark the member wears) or a projection (renderer code). There is no fifth.
N5<N4: Marks classify after resolution; they never resolve.
N6<N1: To the participant they are tiles; in code, cells. Say tiles. Seed is cell.
@5 Pool ~known-location-pools.md sign-meaning-pool-migration-plan.md
P1<N1: A pool of meaning is a directory named sign(meaning) holding records of that meaning. Pools are federated: the local directory is one replica; the same word is the same address on every host.
P2<P1: Derive addresses (Store.poolSignature, getPool); never hardcode hex. Deriving registers the meaning.
P3<P2: The root is an untagged union of lineage bags and pools. Ask the registry (isPoolAddress, poolMeaningOf, poolAddresses, poolMeanings); never keep a local list. Never delete a directory holding 64-hex entries.
P4<P1: Every new meaning carries a colon (family:name). Bare words are reserved and frozen (isReservedPoolWord): refuse them at the naming gesture.
P5<P1: User names never mint root addresses for system purposes; they live one level down inside a known pool.
P6<P1: Pools hold membership or derived state, never truth. Truth stays in layers.
P7<S2: No typed double-underscore folders, ever, and no new one proposed. Legacy ones are drain sources: open without create, read as fallback, never write, never wipe.
@6 Artifact ~website-artifact-paradigm.md
A1<L2: Every artifact is atomic and standalone: it carries what it is and stays valid if any other is deleted. A creation starts as one artifact; to refine it, break it apart into parts that are each artifacts with their own visual. The whole keeps a placeholder per part; an empty placeholder is valid.
A2<A1: No parent or container artifacts. The one sanctioned dependency is a declared interface that belongs to neither side. Nesting tiles in the tile tree is ordinary use, not a container.
A3<A1,N5: A relation is a mark each member wears (group = sign('group:'+meaning), a referent with no bytes behind it). One peer artifact names the relation. Grouping is compatibility: no pairing table. Types interoperate; none depends on another.
A4<A3: A fact about the thing goes in its content record; about the relation, in the group mark (order lives here, never on the member); about the set, in the naming artifact.
A5<A3: Sets nest by enrolling, never containing. A set has no member type. A view renders only the family it owns; a second face is a second view. Family meanings carry a colon.
A6<I1: Share resources, never copy: same content is one signature, stored once, referenced by many.
@7 Derived ~optimize-phase.md
D1<I1: A derived record is a pure derivation of signature-addressed inputs, keyed by the input signature, never by name, path or position. Changed source is a new signature and no record yet: derive on miss, never update.
D2<D1,P6: Derived records live in derived-cache pools. They are recomputable and wipe-safe, never load-bearing: no layer references one, no read path requires one, a cold path gives identical results. Complete or absent, never partial.
D3<D2: Litmus: could a cold client rebuild it from layers alone? Yes: derived cache. No: it is state and needs its own pool of meaning.
D4<D2: Caches are minted only in the optimize phase (idle, after synchronize). Never mint truth there: no layers, markers, lineage writes or gating. synchronize is dispatched only by the processor.
D5<D2: A summary is a derived record keyed by the signature of what it summarises. If summary and subtree disagree, the subtree is truth.
@8 Reach ~install-by-replication.md pools-across-hosts.md intake-filter.md no-third-party-requests.md
T1<I1: Bytes reach a reader by replicate(root), the one verb, from a host. Sharing requires hosting. A relay is a meeting point, not a store.
T2<T1,S3: Verify at admission, never at runtime. Integrity: every atom hashes to its name. Completeness: a tree runs only when its closure has no holes. Authority: a root advances only on a publisher-signed sentinel. After admission runtime trusts the heap.
T3<T2: Never activate a package no followed publisher signed, nor one the shell core cannot serve.
T4<T1: Never push updates. The consumer requests, an icon informs, the human decides.
T5<T1: Three gates, never conflated: selection (whom I take from), intake (what I keep, by marks), activation (what may execute). Publishing and activating are separate choices; holding bytes implies neither.
T6<T1: Carry the selected closure, not a source build. Verify each signature-named byte before use.
T7: Nothing served may make a visitor's browser contact a host we do not control: no font, stylesheet, script, image or preconnect from elsewhere.
@9 Interest ~pheromones.md intake-filter.md
R1<I1: A pheromone is an authored, signed interest-signal deposited on a signature. The author may be a person or an agent that read the content. It travels with the content.
R2<R1,N1: A pheromone never labels what something is: that is the name's job. A new grouping needs a name, never a pheromone kind.
R3<R1: Interests are private and never travel. A match surfaces content; no match is no signal, not a block.
@10 Conduct ~model-mediation-and-the-training-prompt.md anatomy-context-need.md hive-read-fence.md
C1<A6: Pull, do not push: read only what the task needs, expand signatures on demand, within budget. Say when you relied on a summary.
C2<H2: You propose; the participant runs. Never claim a change before the hive reports it ran. Never invent a behaviour name outside the vocabulary you were given.
C3<C2: The doctrine changes only by the participant. You may propose a section through the write fence; it waits for them.
C4<C2: Judge every proposed change against every axiom. A clear break: refuse and cite the id. A doubtful one: wait for the participant.
@11 Build [code] ~CLAUDE.md
B1<P7: Modules (essentials) import only core, never shared, web or dev. The shell loads modules through IoC at runtime. Core holds primitives; essentials holds features.
B2<B1: Externalize everything: a feature is a signed, shareable drone module; the shell only bootstraps. Classification, grouping and rendering live on a molecule name, not in code.
B3<H2: Never wipe or removeEntry user data (root signature files, lineage bags, pools). Verify a change reaches the shell by signature comparison, not by clearing OPFS.
B4<B1: Doctrine ratchets (doctrine.spec.ts) compare against frozen allowlists: never extend one, fix the code. Raw storage writes are frozen per file; durable state goes through the store.
B5<B1: Shell surfaces are registry-fed; never add an hc- tag to app.html. UI text goes through i18n keys.
B6<B1: Private fields use #name; reactivity is EventTarget plus a change event; ESM only with .js relative imports.
B7<N6: Documentation lives only in src/documentation. The retired mirror paradigm is not reintroduced.
